From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gezim <gezimos@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:50:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Kompakt: AOD to on waits for the screen-on block

0020 applies OFF to ON only once the window manager policy unblocks the
screen, so a wake from the sleep screen shows the first real frame. A
wake from AOD went DOZE or DOZE_SUSPEND to ON at once: the policy is
never told, because it was already told ON when AOD started, and the
panel painted the moment between the keyguard going and home being
drawn as a black page.

That wake now goes through the same steps: the policy is told the screen
is turning on, the screen-on block waits for the keyguard (and, on a
wake-and-unlock, 0020's wait for Gone) and for every window to be drawn,
with the policy's own timeouts, and only then is ON applied. Until then
the panel stays in its AOD state.
---
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/DisplayPowerController.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/DisplayPowerController.java
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/DisplayPowerController.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/DisplayPowerController.java
@@ -2224,6 +2224,10 @@
         final boolean changed = mPowerState.getScreenState() != state;
         // Kompakt: see applyScreenStateLocked().
         boolean kompaktApplyAfterPolicy = false;
+        // Kompakt: AOD to ON waits for the policy too, so the panel keeps AOD over the unlock gap.
+        final boolean kompaktFromDoze = isOn && changed
+                && Display.isDozeState(mPowerState.getScreenState())
+                && mReportedScreenStateToPolicy == REPORTED_TO_POLICY_SCREEN_ON;
 
         // If the screen is turning on, give displayoffload a chance to do something before the
         // screen actually turns on.
@@ -2259,7 +2263,8 @@
                 if (isOn
                         && !mDisplayPowerProximityStateController.isScreenOffBecauseOfProximity()
                         && (mPendingScreenOnUnblocker != null
-                                || mReportedScreenStateToPolicy == REPORTED_TO_POLICY_SCREEN_OFF)) {
+                                || mReportedScreenStateToPolicy == REPORTED_TO_POLICY_SCREEN_OFF
+                                || kompaktFromDoze)) {
                     // Kompakt: OFF to ON is applied once the policy unblocks the screen.
                     kompaktApplyAfterPolicy = true;
                 } else {
@@ -2290,9 +2295,10 @@
         }
         if (!isOff
                 && (mReportedScreenStateToPolicy == REPORTED_TO_POLICY_SCREEN_OFF
-                || mReportedScreenStateToPolicy == REPORTED_TO_POLICY_UNREPORTED)) {
+                || mReportedScreenStateToPolicy == REPORTED_TO_POLICY_UNREPORTED
+                || kompaktFromDoze)) {
             setReportedScreenState(REPORTED_TO_POLICY_SCREEN_TURNING_ON);
-            if (mPowerState.getColorFadeLevel() == 0.0f) {
+            if (mPowerState.getColorFadeLevel() == 0.0f || kompaktFromDoze) {
                 blockScreenOn();
             } else {
                 unblockScreenOn();
